GHC 6.2.2 -- mhs: utils/Binary.hs without ByteArray#, S#/J# and :%
Binary (interface-file serialisation) was written against hslibs'
MutableByteArray primitives (newCharArray, readWord8Array, hPutBufBAFull),
GHC's Integer constructors S#/J# (a ByteArray# of limbs), the open Ratio
constructor :% and the old closed IOError type. MicroHs has none of these.
Data.Array.Byte in ST is the same abstraction; Integer is serialised as
sign plus base-256 limbs; Ratio through numerator/denominator; the
FastString dictionary entry is the interned String (the shim FastString
has no ByteArray). Re-implemented rather than emulated (DECISIONS.md D20).
Interface files written this way are read back by the same code, so the
format only has to be self-consistent.

